{"kind":"request","text":"Current R16 browser truth follow-through under existing originaldce, not an architecture or runtime failure claim. Fresh exact34333921844c2055dc774b3d27834b709a73144d lane-forms note line3665 says of a hold ended by time, with unstaged work: 'Hold ended. Work that was not staged is saved privately.' It offers a new hold and restoration of the same holder's checkpoint. This unqualified label is stronger than the adopted R28 lifecycle, which says the checkpoint stays private on hold end and distinguishes acknowledged work, unknown effects and failed recovery. Current same note3707–3711 already requires saved work as acknowledged or not. Recovery's existing4684 further separates stored bytes from a committed checkpoint; that distinction must reach the page, rather than turning a hold-end event into save confirmation.\n\nCorrect the existing Work-view row in the normal dce successor: show the last exact acknowledged checkpoint and what it covers, then later work as not yet saved/pending/unknown or a save failure as actually recorded. If no acknowledged checkpoint exists, say so and offer only authorized recovery/repair/abandon choices that current contracts permit. A new hold may restore only the exact valid acknowledged checkpoint, not silently substitute it for all later unstaged work. Keep unknown command/push/save duties and private-export boundaries under their original identities; no UI promise of survival beyond acknowledged storage evidence, no new checkpoint/host-destruction rule. Suggested labels are conditional: 'Hold ended. Saved work is private: checkpoint C at position n'; 'Hold ended. Later work is not yet confirmed saved', with the actual pending/failure reason.\n\nDistinguishing design examples: successful acknowledged cut before hold end; older checkpoint plus later dirty/untracked/ignored edits and an uncertain save; no checkpoint or refused save after loss/nonstorable root. The same-holder new-hold control must identify exactly which case can restore and any remaining duty. This preserves the original browser experience instead of reducing recovery; not a generated or executed history. Fresh reads were bounded currentR16 row and task-page paragraph, adoptedR28 lifecycle/revocation/receipt excerpts, and effective4684. No whole-R16 reread, source/test/gate/private/provider/browser execution, new task source scope, numeric adoption or priority change. Source remains cc570; forms design8f0d and full original smaller-profile/functionality outcomes remain owed.","body":{"conditions":"The hold-ended Work-view row states exactly what is acknowledged and recoverable, with checkpoint/position evidence, and shows failed/pending/unknown or later-unsaved work distinctly. A hold end alone cannot assert saved work. Same-holder restore uses only the exact valid acknowledged checkpoint; no silent replacement or erased unknown duty. Incorporate in the normal next full lane-forms design review under dce; no new runtime test/gate/probe or new first-Jam gate.","no_git_artifact":"true","priority":"P3 design truth correction within existing dce follow-through; no next-source reprioritization","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}